      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "The goal is to find a number that ends with 952.\n\nI need to find the last digit of this number, which will allow me to find my answer.\nSince any multiple of 22 gives the same remainder as the remainder of the number mod 22, I want to find the remainder when 15 is divided by 22. Because I have found a common multiple of both numbers, this process of division is the same as the modulus operation.\n\n$15 \\div 22 = 0$ remainder $15$. So, the number we need to find ends with $15$.\n\n$15 \\times 100 = 1,500$.\n$1,500 \\equiv 18 \\pmod{22}$ \n$18 \\times 10 = 180$.\n$180 \\equiv 16 \\pmod{22}$\n$16 \\times 100 = 1,600$.\n$1,600 \\equiv 8 \\pmod{22}$.\n$8 \\times 10 = 80$.\n$80 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{22}$.\n$6 \\times 100 = 600$.\n$600 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{22}$.\n$4 \\times 10 = 40$.\n$40 \\equiv 16 \\pmod{22}$.\n$16 \\times 100 = 1,600$.\n$1,600 \\equiv 8 \\pmod{22}$.\n\nCalculating $40 + 600\\ \\%\\ 22\\ = 880 \\pmod{22}$.\n$(10 \\times (40 + 600\\%\\ 22\\))\\% 22\\ = 884$.\n$\\boxed{884}$ is the largest 4 digit integer congruent to $15 \\pmod{22}$. The answer is 884",
