      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The largest 4-digit integer is 9999.\nTo find the largest 4-digit integer congruent to 15 mod 22, we subtract 15 from this number and divide by 22 with a remainder of 1.\n\\[9999 - 15 = 9984,\\]\nso the largest 4-digit integer congruent to 15 mod 22 is $9984 - 22k,$ for some integer $k.$\nWe divide 9984 by 22 and get 458 with a remainder of 16, so the next value is\n\\[9984 - 22(458) = 14\\]\nand we conclude that the largest 4-digit integer congruent to 15 mod 2 satisfies that it must be of the form $9984 - 22k,$ for the largest possible value of $k$ of 22.  Therefore, when $k$ is as large as possible, we have that the largest $4$-digit integer congruent to $15 \\pmod{22}$ is\n\\[9984 - 22(22) = \\boxed{9904}.\\]\nThe answer is: 9904",
